// expect: refuse E_ComputedDelayDepth
// The sayability rule, armed: a feedback line is a fixed set of declared
// slots, so a depth known only at runtime is a depth the medium cannot
// hold. It refuses (nonzero verdict, zero WAT) rather than quietly
// handing this site the one slot it did not ask for.
//
// The sibling of E_ZeroDelayFeedback and the other arm of the same read:
// one projection answers what depth the RHS declares, and the two ways
// that answer can be unusable — zero, and unreadable — are its two
// refusals.
//
// SEEN RED at pin c10ad6ef: this exact program ran, exit 10 — every
// depth silently became one slot, so a computed one looked fine.
//
// A runtime-sized line wants the image-backed sequence rather than a
// register file: Hβ.dataflow.delay-line-runtime-depth. Until it lands,
// saying so is the honest surface.

fn accum(input: Int, n: Int) -> Int =
  ((prev) => input + prev) <~ delay(n - 1)

fn main() -> Int = accum(10, 2)
